      "t": "2026-11-09T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "Russian independent newspaper Novaya Gazeta has ceased operations and closed its Moscow offices, citing pressure from authorities and security services, including restrictions on operations.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-09:12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-09T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "Wikipedia's article on censorship in Russia notes that since 1 November the register of forbidden sites on the Russian segment of the Internet works.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1370578503:154"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-09T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "The Russian constitution prohibits censorship, as stated in paragraph 5 of Article 29.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1370578503:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-09T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "The newspaper's offices were in Moscow, Russia, the location the reports give.",
